{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1334562-bloodlines-2-best-thinblood-disciplines-by-clan","id":1334562,"title":"Bloodlines 2: Best Thinblood Disciplines by Clan","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-08T18:09:33-07:00","id":1334562,"title":"Bloodlines 2: Best Thinblood Disciplines by Clan","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CP7mf8ieirU\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CP7mf8ieirU\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CP7mf8ieirU\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CP7mf8ieirU </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25564-secret_dowwe","name":"secret_dowwe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T21:24:53-07:00","id":1334579,"title":"","content":"Personally, I've decided to wield the following.<br /> <br /> <b>Malkavian - Nebulation:</b> I feel like the mist powers would compliment the sense of creeping madness the clan gives off.<br /> <br /> <b>Tremere - Mentalism:</b> Once again, I feel like telekinetic powers would compliment the sense of occult mysticism the clan gives off.<br /> <br /> <b>Ventrue - Chiropteran:</b> The classic image of a vampire Lord gliding above the city, and commanding a swarm of bats seems like it would be appropriate for a game that allows for vampire parkour.<br /> <br /> <b>Brujah - Nebulation:</b> No particular role play aesthetic here. But combining the mist powers with the Brujah's supernatural agility and strength, I feel like this choice would make for an extremely deadly combat focused character.<br /> <br /> <b>Toreador - Mentalism:</b> If I'm going to play as a pretty boy, harem king vampire, then I'm going to go full anime with it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T17:24:28-07:00","id":1335224,"title":"","content":"Ooh! I like the misty Malkavian &quot;creeping madness.&quot; And Mentalism is a good lore-consistent discipline for Tremere. I feel like it pushes their Auspex further.<br /> <br /> I could see the old school vamp-lord bat thing being cool. Also, I now want vamp-arkour--so thanks for that.<br /> <br /> Misty Brujah? Nah, bro. I think it'll slow them down. Unless they can be potent speedy mist.<br /> <br /> Ha! Tore-adorable. I never play Toreador. Don't know why. Feel like I'd be betraying my Nossie soul, I guess.<br /> <br /> Cheers, mate!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25564-secret_dowwe","name":"secret_dowwe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-12T07:28:54-07:00","id":1335307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>secret_dowwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1334562-bloodlines-2-best-thinblood-disciplines-by-clan?p=1335224#post1335224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Misty Brujah? Nah, bro. I think it'll slow them down. Unless they can be potent speedy mist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rememer, one of Nebulation's abilities lets you create a cloud of choking mist to incapacitate your foes. <br /> <br /> Drop one of those on a cluster of enemies, then go to town on them with Potence and Celerity. They'll all be dead before the mist clears! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T07:02:36-07:00","id":1335491,"title":"","content":"What thinblood disciplines you think is better for ventrue and toreador?<br /> Also ventrue or toreador looks more like the major hero of bloodlines 2 ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T08:16:37-07:00","id":1335509,"title":"","content":"I think Mentalism for Toreador and Nebulation for Ventrue. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1394\" data-vbnamecard=\"1394\">Nyrufa</a> had other ideas I thought were really good. I think it's mostly about how you want to play, and that most anything can be made to work.<br /> <br /> One of my favorite things about VtM and WoD is that there aren't really heroes. A lot of games I play, I feel like I get pigeon-holed into being a certain way. Even if the game play's great, I have to accept that altruistic character's reasons for doing anything at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25564-secret_dowwe","name":"secret_dowwe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}